    "391": {
      "date": "2026-09-21",
      "edition": "Monday 21 September",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "WXV Global Series",
          "heading": "Wales women deliver statement performance in eight-try demolition of South Africa",
          "body": "The Wales women's side secured an emphatic 50-19 victory over South Africa in their WXV Global Series opener at Cardiff Arms Park. Head coach Sean Lynn praised his squad's new DNA, noting the significant growth in skill development that underpinned their dominant eight-try performance. Co-captain Alex Callender earned player of the match honours, while Sisilia Tuipulotu impressed with a brace of tries. “This is just the start for us, this is going to be our new DNA,” Lynn said following the result."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
